# =============================================================================
# Path compression on a byte-ART node, term = "metamorphosis".
# Source of truth: src/persistent_artrie/nodes/mod.rs (MAX_PREFIX_LEN = 12) and
# core::overlay::codec::chain_chunks (multi-node chunking when a chain exceeds
# the inline cap).
#
# BEFORE: a unary chain — one node per byte (14 nodes for one string).
# AFTER : the single-child run collapses into ONE node carrying an inline
#         partial prefix (byte variant: up to 12 bytes inline; the first 8 are
#         pessimistically compared during descent, the remainder verified at the
#         leaf). The whole word fits one inline prefix, so the chain becomes a
#         single final node.
#
# Color key (rendered by the wrapper):
#   blue = persistent / disk-backed node   ·   green = the collapsed final node
# =============================================================================

  BEFORE  —  uncompressed unary chain (14 nodes)

  (root)
    |  'm'
    v
   (m)-'e'->(e)-'t'->(t)-'a'->(a)-'m'->(m)-'o'->(o)-'r'->(r)
                                                            |
                                            'p','h','o','s','i'
                                                            v
                                          ...->(i)-'s'-> ( s* )   * = final

  Each edge is a separate node => up to 14 page faults to read one word.


  AFTER  —  single-child run collapsed into one inline-prefix node (1 node)

  (root)
    |  'm'
    v
  +--------------------------------------------------+
  | partial = "metamorphosi"   (12 bytes inline)     |   * final
  | partial_len = 13  (> 12: tail 's' verified at     |
  |                    the leaf; first 8 pessimistic) |
  +--------------------------------------------------+

  Saving: 14 nodes -> 1 node; up to 14 page faults -> 1 (or 2 on tail verify).
  A run longer than 12 inline bytes is chunked into ceil(len / 13) such nodes
  (chain_chunks, proven never to truncate), never a 1-node-per-byte chain.
